NODE : Reporter
TITLE: Final Report

LangChain implements its callback system through a structured architecture defined in `langchain_core.callbacks`. The implementation relies on two primary components:

*   **`BaseCallbackHandler`** (defined in `libs/core/langchain_core/callbacks/base.py`): This serves as the interface for listening to events within LangChain. Handlers are designed to react to specific lifecycle events (such as the start or end of an LLM call, chain execution, or tool usage).
*   **`CallbackManager`** (defined in `libs/core/langchain_core/callbacks/manager.py`): This acts as the orchestrator. It manages the registration of callback handlers and triggers the appropriate methods on those handlers during the execution lifecycle of LangChain components.

By registering handlers with a `CallbackManager`, users can hook into various events throughout the execution flow, allowing for logging, tracing, or custom logic integration.

